[2026-03-14T22:45:18.748Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EVMYksRbiRQGdDtrrt9WJq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UGzzsJ7HNdHxwY1bQ5myuv","name":"Grep","input":{"pattern":"booking.*action|cancel.*booking|confirm.*booking|host.*dashboard.*booking","path":"/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/docs/tests.md","output_mode":"content","-i":true,"-C":5},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2752,"cache_read_input_tokens":32120,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2752,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2246777-4cd6-42ce-8777-30d908ca9f10","uuid":"9b798f7b-ca42-442f-aad9-abfb969c33d9"}
[2026-03-14T22:45:18.784Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGzzsJ7HNdHxwY1bQ5myuv","type":"tool_result","content":"528-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n529-- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n530-- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set guests to 0 or a negative number.\n531-\n532-#### Test: Reserve button shows error for unavailable dates\n533:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on a property detail page. The property has an existing confirmed booking for \"2026-05-01\" to \"2026-05-04\".\n534-- **Action:** User selects overlapping dates (e.g., check-in \"2026-05-02\", check-out \"2026-05-06\") and clicks \"Reserve\".\n535-- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Property is not available for the selected dates\"). The booking is not created.\n536-\n537-#### Test: Booking card is sticky on desktop viewport\n538-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page on a desktop viewport.\n--\n597-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has bio set to null.\n598-- **Expected:** The host info card displays the host name, avatar, and member since date. The bio area is either not shown or displays a default message. No empty or broken layout.\n599-\n600-## Page: My Trips (`/trips`)\n601-\n602:<!-- Components: TripsTabs, TripCard, CancelBookingDialog -->\n603-\n604-### Component: TripsTabs\n605-\n606-#### Test: My Trips page requires login\n607-- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n608-- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips`.\n609-- **Expected:** The user is redirected to the login page (`/login`). The My Trips page content is not displayed.\n610-\n611-#### Test: My Trips page defaults to Upcoming tab\n612-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips`.\n613:- **Expected:** The page displays three tabs: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Cancelled\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected/highlighted by default. The content area shows upcoming trips (bookings with status \"pending\" or \"confirmed\" and check_in date >= today).\n614-\n615:#### Test: Upcoming tab shows pending and confirmed future bookings\n616:- **Initial state:** User is logged in with bookings: a confirmed booking checking in next week, a pending booking checking in next month, a completed booking from last month, and a cancelled booking.\n617-- **Action:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n618:- **Expected:** Only the confirmed and pending future bookings are displayed. Completed and cancelled bookings are not shown in this tab.\n619-\n620-#### Test: Switching to Past tab shows completed bookings\n621-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has completed bookings.\n622-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n623:- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"completed\". Upcoming and cancelled bookings are not shown.\n624-\n625:#### Test: Switching to Cancelled tab shows cancelled bookings\n626:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has cancelled bookings.\n627-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n628:- **Expected:** The \"Cancelled\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"cancelled\". Upcoming and completed bookings are not shown.\n629-\n630-#### Test: Switching back to Upcoming tab from another tab\n631-- **Initial state:** User is on the My Trips page with the \"Past\" tab selected.\n632-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n633-- **Expected:** The \"Upcoming\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show upcoming bookings again.\n--\n636-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no completed bookings.\n637-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n638-- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab content area displays a message like \"No past trips\" or \"You don't have any past trips yet.\" instead of an empty list.\n639-\n640-#### Test: Upcoming tab empty state message\n641:- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no pending or confirmed future bookings.\n642-- **Action:** User views the \"Upcoming\" tab (default).\n643-- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No upcoming trips\" with a suggestion to browse properties (e.g., a link to the home page).\n644-\n645-#### Test: Cancelled tab empty state message\n646:- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no cancelled bookings.\n647-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n648-- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No cancelled trips.\"\n649-\n650-#### Test: Tabs are functional on repeated use\n651-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page.\n--\n669-#### Test: Clicking trip card navigates to booking details\n670-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A trip card is displayed for a booking with id \"booking-123\".\n671-- **Action:** User clicks on the trip card (not the cancel or review button).\n672-- **Expected:** The app navigates to a booking detail view showing full booking information including property details, dates, guest count, price breakdown, and special requests.\n673-\n674:#### Test: Cancel button appears on pending bookings\n675-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"pending\" is displayed.\n676-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button (or cancel icon button) that is clickable.\n677-\n678:#### Test: Cancel button appears on confirmed bookings\n679-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n680-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button that is clickable.\n681-\n682:#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on completed bookings\n683-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" is displayed.\n684-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n685-\n686:#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on already cancelled bookings\n687:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Cancelled\" tab. A booking with status \"cancelled\" is displayed.\n688-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n689-\n690-#### Test: Write Review button appears on completed bookings without a review\n691-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" exists that does not have an associated review.\n692-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Write Review\" button that is clickable.\n--\n698-#### Test: Clicking Write Review button navigates to review page\n699-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking with id \"booking-456\" has no review.\n700-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Write Review\" button on that trip card.\n701-- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/trips/booking-456/review` (the Write Review page).\n702-\n703:#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on pending, confirmed, or cancelled bookings\n704-- **Initial state:** User is logged in. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"cancelled\".\n705-- **Expected:** None of these trip cards display a \"Write Review\" button. The button only appears for \"completed\" bookings.\n706-\n707-#### Test: Trip cards are ordered by check-in date\n708-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. Multiple upcoming bookings exist with different check-in dates.\n709-- **Expected:** Trip cards are displayed in chronological order by check-in date, with the soonest upcoming trip first.\n710-\n711:### Component: CancelBookingDialog\n712-\n713-#### Test: Clicking Cancel button opens confirmation dialog\n714-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed with a \"Cancel\" button.\n715-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card.\n716:- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog/modal appears asking the user to confirm the cancellation. The dialog displays text like \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\" with the property name and dates for context. Two buttons are visible: \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") and \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\").\n717-\n718:#### Test: Confirming cancellation updates booking status to cancelled\n719:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a confirmed booking.\n720-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") button.\n721:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab (or its status badge updates to \"Cancelled\" in red). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking cancelled successfully\"). The booking now appears in the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n722-\n723:#### Test: Dismissing cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n724:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n725-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\") button.\n726-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking remains in its original status (pending). No API call is made. The trip card is unchanged.\n727-\n728-#### Test: Closing the dialog via overlay click keeps booking unchanged\n729-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open.\n730-- **Action:** User clicks outside the dialog (on the overlay/backdrop).\n731-- **Expected:** The dialog closes without making any changes to the booking.\n732-\n733-#### Test: Cancel dialog shows property and date context\n734-- **Initial state:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on a trip card for property \"Mountain Cabin\" with dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\".\n735:- **Expected:** The confirmation dialog displays the property name \"Mountain Cabin\" and the booking dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\" so the user can confirm they are cancelling the correct booking.\n736-\n737:#### Test: After cancellation, booking moves from Upcoming to Cancelled tab\n738:- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with a confirmed booking for \"Beach House\".\n739-- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the \"Beach House\" trip card, then confirms the cancellation in the dialog.\n740:- **Expected:** The \"Beach House\" trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab. User switches to the \"Cancelled\" tab and sees the \"Beach House\" booking with a red \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n741-\n742-#### Test: Cancel dialog is functional on repeated use\n743:- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with two cancellable bookings.\n744:- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the first booking, dismisses the dialog (clicks \"Keep Booking\"), then clicks \"Cancel\" on the second booking and confirms the cancellation.\n745-- **Expected:** The first booking remains unchanged in the \"Upcoming\" tab. The second booking is cancelled and moves to the \"Cancelled\" tab. Each dialog open/close cycle works correctly.\n746-\n747-## Page: Host Dashboard (`/hosting`)\n748-\n749-<!-- Components: StatsOverview, ListingsTab, BookingsTab, AddListingForm -->\n--\n766-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Listings\" stat card showing \"5\" (only active listings counted). The card has a label \"Total Listings\" and a numeric value.\n767-\n768-#### Test: Stats overview displays active bookings count\n769-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have 3 bookings with status \"confirmed\", 2 with status \"pending\", and 4 with status \"completed\".\n770-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n771:- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Active Bookings\" stat card showing \"5\" (pending + confirmed bookings). The card has a label \"Active Bookings\" and a numeric value.\n772-\n773-#### Test: Stats overview displays total earnings\n774-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have completed bookings with total_price values of $500, $750, and $1200.\n775-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n776-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Earnings\" stat card showing \"$2,450\" (sum of completed booking total prices). The value is formatted as currency.\n--\n783-#### Test: Stats overview shows zeros for a new host with no data\n784-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties, no bookings, and no reviews.\n785-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n786-- **Expected:** All four stat cards display zero/empty values: \"Total Listings: 0\", \"Active Bookings: 0\", \"Total Earnings: $0\", and \"Average Rating: —\" (or \"N/A\" when no reviews exist).\n787-\n788:#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n789-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n790-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n791-- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n792-\n793-#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n--\n865-- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"pending\" are displayed in the table. The \"Pending\" filter appears active/selected.\n866-\n867-#### Test: Filtering bookings by Confirmed status\n868-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n869-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirmed\" status filter.\n870:- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"confirmed\" are shown. Other bookings are hidden.\n871-\n872-#### Test: Filtering bookings by Completed status\n873-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n874-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Completed\" status filter.\n875-- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"completed\" are shown.\n--\n887-#### Test: Status filters work on repeated use\n888-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n889-- **Action:** User clicks \"Pending\", then \"Confirmed\", then \"All\", then \"Completed\".\n890-- **Expected:** Each filter correctly shows the appropriate subset of bookings. The active filter indicator updates correctly each time.\n891-\n892:#### Test: Host can confirm a pending booking\n893-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"pending\" for guest \"Bob\" at property \"Beach House\" is displayed.\n894:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm\" button on that booking row.\n895:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"confirmed\". The booking's status badge changes from yellow \"Pending\" to green \"Confirmed\". The \"Confirm\" button is no longer visible for that booking. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking confirmed\"). The \"Active Bookings\" stat in StatsOverview remains accurate.\n896-\n897:#### Test: Host can cancel a pending booking\n898-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A pending booking is displayed.\n899:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the pending booking row.\n900-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking the host to confirm cancellation. The dialog shows the guest name, property, and dates for context.\n901-\n902:#### Test: Confirming cancellation of a booking updates status\n903:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n904-- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button in the dialog.\n905:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The booking's status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" action buttons are removed for that booking. A success message is displayed. The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases by 1.\n906-\n907:#### Test: Dismissing booking cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n908:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a booking.\n909-- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss button or clicks outside the dialog.\n910-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking status remains unchanged.\n911-\n912:#### Test: Host can cancel a confirmed booking\n913-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n914:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the confirmed booking row and confirms in the dialog.\n915:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases.\n916-\n917:#### Test: Completed and cancelled bookings have no action buttons\n918-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"completed\" and \"cancelled\".\n919:- **Expected:** Booking rows with \"completed\" or \"cancelled\" status do not display \"Confirm\" or \"Cancel\" action buttons. Only pending and confirmed bookings show action buttons.\n920-\n921-#### Test: Bookings tab shows empty state when no bookings exist\n922-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with properties but no bookings.\n923-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n924-- **Expected:** The tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"No bookings yet\").\n--\n927-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with bookings in all four statuses.\n928-- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" has a yellow badge, \"Confirmed\" has a green badge, \"Cancelled\" has a red badge, \"Completed\" has a blue badge.\n929-\n930-#### Test: Confirm and cancel actions work on repeated use\n931-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with three pending bookings.\n932:- **Action:** User confirms the first booking, cancels the second booking (confirming the dialog), and then confirms the third booking.\n933:- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct booking. The first and third show \"Confirmed\" badges, the second shows \"Cancelled\". Stats update correctly after each action.\n934-\n935-### Component: AddListingForm\n936-\n937-#### Test: Clicking Add Listing button opens the multi-step form\n938-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Listings tab."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2246777-4cd6-42ce-8777-30d908ca9f10","uuid":"c673db61-593b-40bd-90a1-eb9ed786108c","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"528-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n529-- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n530-- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set guests to 0 or a negative number.\n531-\n532-#### Test: Reserve button shows error for unavailable dates\n533:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on a property detail page. The property has an existing confirmed booking for \"2026-05-01\" to \"2026-05-04\".\n534-- **Action:** User selects overlapping dates (e.g., check-in \"2026-05-02\", check-out \"2026-05-06\") and clicks \"Reserve\".\n535-- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Property is not available for the selected dates\"). The booking is not created.\n536-\n537-#### Test: Booking card is sticky on desktop viewport\n538-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page on a desktop viewport.\n--\n597-- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has bio set to null.\n598-- **Expected:** The host info card displays the host name, avatar, and member since date. The bio area is either not shown or displays a default message. No empty or broken layout.\n599-\n600-## Page: My Trips (`/trips`)\n601-\n602:<!-- Components: TripsTabs, TripCard, CancelBookingDialog -->\n603-\n604-### Component: TripsTabs\n605-\n606-#### Test: My Trips page requires login\n607-- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n608-- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips`.\n609-- **Expected:** The user is redirected to the login page (`/login`). The My Trips page content is not displayed.\n610-\n611-#### Test: My Trips page defaults to Upcoming tab\n612-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips`.\n613:- **Expected:** The page displays three tabs: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Cancelled\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected/highlighted by default. The content area shows upcoming trips (bookings with status \"pending\" or \"confirmed\" and check_in date >= today).\n614-\n615:#### Test: Upcoming tab shows pending and confirmed future bookings\n616:- **Initial state:** User is logged in with bookings: a confirmed booking checking in next week, a pending booking checking in next month, a completed booking from last month, and a cancelled booking.\n617-- **Action:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n618:- **Expected:** Only the confirmed and pending future bookings are displayed. Completed and cancelled bookings are not shown in this tab.\n619-\n620-#### Test: Switching to Past tab shows completed bookings\n621-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has completed bookings.\n622-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n623:- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"completed\". Upcoming and cancelled bookings are not shown.\n624-\n625:#### Test: Switching to Cancelled tab shows cancelled bookings\n626:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has cancelled bookings.\n627-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n628:- **Expected:** The \"Cancelled\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"cancelled\". Upcoming and completed bookings are not shown.\n629-\n630-#### Test: Switching back to Upcoming tab from another tab\n631-- **Initial state:** User is on the My Trips page with the \"Past\" tab selected.\n632-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n633-- **Expected:** The \"Upcoming\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show upcoming bookings again.\n--\n636-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no completed bookings.\n637-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n638-- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab content area displays a message like \"No past trips\" or \"You don't have any past trips yet.\" instead of an empty list.\n639-\n640-#### Test: Upcoming tab empty state message\n641:- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no pending or confirmed future bookings.\n642-- **Action:** User views the \"Upcoming\" tab (default).\n643-- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No upcoming trips\" with a suggestion to browse properties (e.g., a link to the home page).\n644-\n645-#### Test: Cancelled tab empty state message\n646:- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no cancelled bookings.\n647-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n648-- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No cancelled trips.\"\n649-\n650-#### Test: Tabs are functional on repeated use\n651-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page.\n--\n669-#### Test: Clicking trip card navigates to booking details\n670-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A trip card is displayed for a booking with id \"booking-123\".\n671-- **Action:** User clicks on the trip card (not the cancel or review button).\n672-- **Expected:** The app navigates to a booking detail view showing full booking information including property details, dates, guest count, price breakdown, and special requests.\n673-\n674:#### Test: Cancel button appears on pending bookings\n675-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"pending\" is displayed.\n676-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button (or cancel icon button) that is clickable.\n677-\n678:#### Test: Cancel button appears on confirmed bookings\n679-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n680-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button that is clickable.\n681-\n682:#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on completed bookings\n683-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" is displayed.\n684-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n685-\n686:#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on already cancelled bookings\n687:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Cancelled\" tab. A booking with status \"cancelled\" is displayed.\n688-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n689-\n690-#### Test: Write Review button appears on completed bookings without a review\n691-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" exists that does not have an associated review.\n692-- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Write Review\" button that is clickable.\n--\n698-#### Test: Clicking Write Review button navigates to review page\n699-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking with id \"booking-456\" has no review.\n700-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Write Review\" button on that trip card.\n701-- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/trips/booking-456/review` (the Write Review page).\n702-\n703:#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on pending, confirmed, or cancelled bookings\n704-- **Initial state:** User is logged in. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"cancelled\".\n705-- **Expected:** None of these trip cards display a \"Write Review\" button. The button only appears for \"completed\" bookings.\n706-\n707-#### Test: Trip cards are ordered by check-in date\n708-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. Multiple upcoming bookings exist with different check-in dates.\n709-- **Expected:** Trip cards are displayed in chronological order by check-in date, with the soonest upcoming trip first.\n710-\n711:### Component: CancelBookingDialog\n712-\n713-#### Test: Clicking Cancel button opens confirmation dialog\n714-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed with a \"Cancel\" button.\n715-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card.\n716:- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog/modal appears asking the user to confirm the cancellation. The dialog displays text like \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\" with the property name and dates for context. Two buttons are visible: \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") and \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\").\n717-\n718:#### Test: Confirming cancellation updates booking status to cancelled\n719:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a confirmed booking.\n720-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") button.\n721:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab (or its status badge updates to \"Cancelled\" in red). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking cancelled successfully\"). The booking now appears in the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n722-\n723:#### Test: Dismissing cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n724:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n725-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\") button.\n726-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking remains in its original status (pending). No API call is made. The trip card is unchanged.\n727-\n728-#### Test: Closing the dialog via overlay click keeps booking unchanged\n729-- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open.\n730-- **Action:** User clicks outside the dialog (on the overlay/backdrop).\n731-- **Expected:** The dialog closes without making any changes to the booking.\n732-\n733-#### Test: Cancel dialog shows property and date context\n734-- **Initial state:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on a trip card for property \"Mountain Cabin\" with dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\".\n735:- **Expected:** The confirmation dialog displays the property name \"Mountain Cabin\" and the booking dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\" so the user can confirm they are cancelling the correct booking.\n736-\n737:#### Test: After cancellation, booking moves from Upcoming to Cancelled tab\n738:- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with a confirmed booking for \"Beach House\".\n739-- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the \"Beach House\" trip card, then confirms the cancellation in the dialog.\n740:- **Expected:** The \"Beach House\" trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab. User switches to the \"Cancelled\" tab and sees the \"Beach House\" booking with a red \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n741-\n742-#### Test: Cancel dialog is functional on repeated use\n743:- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with two cancellable bookings.\n744:- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the first booking, dismisses the dialog (clicks \"Keep Booking\"), then clicks \"Cancel\" on the second booking and confirms the cancellation.\n745-- **Expected:** The first booking remains unchanged in the \"Upcoming\" tab. The second booking is cancelled and moves to the \"Cancelled\" tab. Each dialog open/close cycle works correctly.\n746-\n747-## Page: Host Dashboard (`/hosting`)\n748-\n749-<!-- Components: StatsOverview, ListingsTab, BookingsTab, AddListingForm -->\n--\n766-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Listings\" stat card showing \"5\" (only active listings counted). The card has a label \"Total Listings\" and a numeric value.\n767-\n768-#### Test: Stats overview displays active bookings count\n769-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have 3 bookings with status \"confirmed\", 2 with status \"pending\", and 4 with status \"completed\".\n770-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n771:- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Active Bookings\" stat card showing \"5\" (pending + confirmed bookings). The card has a label \"Active Bookings\" and a numeric value.\n772-\n773-#### Test: Stats overview displays total earnings\n774-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have completed bookings with total_price values of $500, $750, and $1200.\n775-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n776-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Earnings\" stat card showing \"$2,450\" (sum of completed booking total prices). The value is formatted as currency.\n--\n783-#### Test: Stats overview shows zeros for a new host with no data\n784-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties, no bookings, and no reviews.\n785-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n786-- **Expected:** All four stat cards display zero/empty values: \"Total Listings: 0\", \"Active Bookings: 0\", \"Total Earnings: $0\", and \"Average Rating: —\" (or \"N/A\" when no reviews exist).\n787-\n788:#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n789-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n790-- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n791-- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n792-\n793-#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n--\n865-- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"pending\" are displayed in the table. The \"Pending\" filter appears active/selected.\n866-\n867-#### Test: Filtering bookings by Confirmed status\n868-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n869-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirmed\" status filter.\n870:- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"confirmed\" are shown. Other bookings are hidden.\n871-\n872-#### Test: Filtering bookings by Completed status\n873-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n874-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Completed\" status filter.\n875-- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"completed\" are shown.\n--\n887-#### Test: Status filters work on repeated use\n888-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n889-- **Action:** User clicks \"Pending\", then \"Confirmed\", then \"All\", then \"Completed\".\n890-- **Expected:** Each filter correctly shows the appropriate subset of bookings. The active filter indicator updates correctly each time.\n891-\n892:#### Test: Host can confirm a pending booking\n893-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"pending\" for guest \"Bob\" at property \"Beach House\" is displayed.\n894:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm\" button on that booking row.\n895:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"confirmed\". The booking's status badge changes from yellow \"Pending\" to green \"Confirmed\". The \"Confirm\" button is no longer visible for that booking. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking confirmed\"). The \"Active Bookings\" stat in StatsOverview remains accurate.\n896-\n897:#### Test: Host can cancel a pending booking\n898-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A pending booking is displayed.\n899:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the pending booking row.\n900-- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking the host to confirm cancellation. The dialog shows the guest name, property, and dates for context.\n901-\n902:#### Test: Confirming cancellation of a booking updates status\n903:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n904-- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button in the dialog.\n905:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The booking's status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" action buttons are removed for that booking. A success message is displayed. The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases by 1.\n906-\n907:#### Test: Dismissing booking cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n908:- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a booking.\n909-- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss button or clicks outside the dialog.\n910-- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking status remains unchanged.\n911-\n912:#### Test: Host can cancel a confirmed booking\n913-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n914:- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the confirmed booking row and confirms in the dialog.\n915:- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases.\n916-\n917:#### Test: Completed and cancelled bookings have no action buttons\n918-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"completed\" and \"cancelled\".\n919:- **Expected:** Booking rows with \"completed\" or \"cancelled\" status do not display \"Confirm\" or \"Cancel\" action buttons. Only pending and confirmed bookings show action buttons.\n920-\n921-#### Test: Bookings tab shows empty state when no bookings exist\n922-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with properties but no bookings.\n923-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n924-- **Expected:** The tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"No bookings yet\").\n--\n927-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with bookings in all four statuses.\n928-- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" has a yellow badge, \"Confirmed\" has a green badge, \"Cancelled\" has a red badge, \"Completed\" has a blue badge.\n929-\n930-#### Test: Confirm and cancel actions work on repeated use\n931-- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with three pending bookings.\n932:- **Action:** User confirms the first booking, cancels the second booking (confirming the dialog), and then confirms the third booking.\n933:- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct booking. The first and third show \"Confirmed\" badges, the second shows \"Cancelled\". Stats update correctly after each action.\n934-\n935-### Component: AddListingForm\n936-\n937-#### Test: Clicking Add Listing button opens the multi-step form\n938-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Listings tab.","numLines":232}}
